/ethindp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ethindp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ethindp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ethindp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-12T22:34:29Z","updated_at":"2026-03-12T22:34:29Z","body":"@bruvzg This is looking almost perfect! The only thing I think your doing wrong is in the URL handling: instead of presenting the link text, your dumping the raw URL and text in sequence.\r\n\r\nWhat are your thoughts on this? I'm thinking of a fallback process: render URL text if present, otherwise the raw URL. Although that begs the question of if the Godot documentation has anything like `[url=url_goes_here]this[/url]` or similar. If it does, that might not be a smart thing to do. On the other hand, the links in the rendered speech technically qualify as noise. This is pretty much my only nitpick with it (and even then it's a small one).","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4050666220/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4053155093","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117358#issuecomment-4053155093","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117358","id":4053155093,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7xlj0V","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/b